{"question": "Your embedding model's documentation says to prefix inputs with \"query:\" and \"passage:\" (or to use a separate query instruction). What happens if you skip this, and why does it matter?", "topic": "RAG", "subtopic": "embeddings", "difficulty": "basic", "skills": ["metric evaluation", "query-document matching", "embedding performance"], "expected_concepts": ["asymmetric query vs document embeddings", "retrieval success metrics", "interpretation of results"], "follow_up_topics": ["embedding evaluation techniques", "user feedback mechanisms", "comparison with baseline models"], "evaluation_criteria": ["Names precision and recall as key metrics", "Explains how to interpret precision and recall in this context", "Discusses differences in performance expectation based on embedding type"], "id": "q_8109ddd2ce", "source": "llm_generated", "review_status": "approved", "reference_answer": {"key_points": ["Many retrieval embedding models are trained asymmetrically: short queries and long passages are encoded differently, using prefixes, instructions or separate query and document encoders", "Skipping the prefix or instruction means queries and documents land in a less well-aligned space, which lowers similarity quality and recall", "The prefixes must be applied consistently, queries with the query prefix and documents with the document prefix, and the same way at indexing time and query time", "Mixing up the two or applying the wrong one is a silent failure: the system still returns results, just worse ones", "Symmetric tasks (finding similar documents) use the same encoding on both sides, so check the model card for which mode your task needs", "Confirm the effect by comparing recall@k on a golden question set with and without the prefixes"], "common_mistakes": ["Confusing precision with accuracy, which can lead to misinterpretation of retrieval success.", "Neglecting to consider the context of the embeddings when interpreting metrics.", "Failing to account for the trade-off between recall and precision in asymmetric embeddings."]}, "follow_up_questions": ["What specific datasets would you use for evaluation?", "How would you handle cases of ambiguous queries?", "Can you explain how you would visualize these metrics for stakeholders?"]}
