{"question": "Your team is considering re-indexing after an upgrade to the embedding model; what realistic failure modes could occur without this step, and how would you detect them?", "topic": "RAG", "subtopic": "embeddings", "difficulty": "advanced", "skills": ["re-indexing", "failure detection", "model upgrade"], "expected_concepts": ["re-indexing importance", "realistic failure modes", "detection mechanisms"], "follow_up_topics": ["upgrade strategies", "rollback procedures", "impact analysis"], "evaluation_criteria": ["Names re-indexing importance as a core concept", "Identifies realistic failure modes due to lack of re-indexing", "Discusses specific detection mechanisms for issues"], "id": "q_4d5af7e29f", "source": "llm_generated", "review_status": "approved", "reference_answer": {"key_points": ["Embeddings from different models or versions are not comparable: if queries use the new model but the index holds old vectors, similarity scores are meaningless and the results are poor", "If the new model has a different dimension, queries fail with errors; if the dimension is the same, it fails silently and just returns bad results, which is harder to catch", "A partial re-index leaves a mixed index with both old and new vectors, so ranking becomes inconsistent and some documents are effectively unfindable", "Detect it by comparing recall@k and MRR on a golden question set before and after the upgrade, and by watching for sudden drops in similarity scores or in click or answer quality", "Store the embedding model name and version as metadata on every vector so you can verify the whole index matches the query model", "Safe rollout: build a new index in parallel (blue-green), validate it, then switch with an alias, and keep the old index for rollback"], "common_mistakes": ["Assuming that the new model will automatically improve results without re-indexing.", "Neglecting to consider the impact of embedding drift over time.", "Overlooking the importance of monitoring and evaluation after the upgrade."]}, "follow_up_questions": ["What specific metrics would you use to evaluate the performance of the new embeddings?", "How would you handle the re-indexing process to minimize downtime?", "Can you describe a scenario where re-indexing was critical in your past projects?"]}
