{"question": "During a production rollout, you notice that the evaluation metrics for your retrieval system are drifting unexpectedly. How would you determine if this is due to evaluation set drift, and what steps would you take to investigate and address the issue?", "topic": "RAG", "subtopic": "retrieval evaluation", "difficulty": "advanced", "skills": ["evaluation set drift", "metric tracking", "data analysis"], "expected_concepts": ["evaluation set drift", "historical performance comparison", "data quality assessment"], "follow_up_topics": ["analyzing data sources", "performance benchmarking", "establishing baselines"], "evaluation_criteria": ["Defines evaluation set drift clearly", "Mentions historical performance comparison", "Outlines measures to assess data quality"], "id": "q_acf9b8921d", "source": "llm_generated", "review_status": "pending", "reference_answer": {"key_points": ["Analyze historical performance metrics to identify trends over time and pinpoint when the drift began.", "Conduct a statistical analysis of the evaluation set to check for changes in distribution or characteristics compared to the training set.", "Implement data quality checks to ensure that the evaluation set has not been compromised by issues such as labeling errors or data corruption."], "common_mistakes": ["Failing to compare the evaluation set with the training set to identify distribution shifts.", "Not considering external factors that may have influenced user behavior or data collection methods."]}, "follow_up_questions": ["What specific statistical tests would you use to assess distribution changes?", "How would you handle a situation where the evaluation set is confirmed to have drifted?", "What tools or frameworks do you recommend for monitoring retrieval system performance over time?"]}
