{"question": "If you were tasked with designing an offline test plan to evaluate two different retrieval algorithms under the constraint of processing time, what key factors would you consider, and how would you ensure your evaluation is robust?", "topic": "RAG", "subtopic": "retrieval evaluation", "difficulty": "advanced", "skills": ["offline evaluation", "algorithm comparison", "test design"], "expected_concepts": ["offline evaluation vs online A/B testing", "test coverage", "performance consistency"], "follow_up_topics": ["real-world application scenarios", "metrics for online performance", "scalability concerns"], "evaluation_criteria": ["Explains the differences between offline evaluation and A/B testing", "Outlines essential metrics for robust evaluation", "Considers test coverage in algorithm assessment"], "id": "q_d99ce3b73b", "source": "llm_generated", "review_status": "pending", "reference_answer": {"key_points": ["Define clear metrics for evaluation such as precision, recall, and F1 score to assess retrieval effectiveness.", "Ensure a diverse and representative dataset that covers various query types and user intents to avoid bias.", "Incorporate processing time as a constraint by measuring the latency of each algorithm under different load conditions.", "Use statistical significance tests to validate the results and ensure that observed differences are not due to random chance.", "Implement cross-validation techniques to assess the robustness of the algorithms across different subsets of the data."], "common_mistakes": ["Neglecting to define specific evaluation metrics, leading to ambiguous results.", "Using a non-representative dataset that does not reflect real-world usage scenarios.", "Failing to account for variability in processing time across different runs."]}, "follow_up_questions": ["What specific metrics would you prioritize for retrieval effectiveness?", "How would you handle potential biases in your dataset?", "Can you describe a method for ensuring statistical significance in your results?"]}
{"question": "If you need to debug a production failure where the retrieval system is not meeting the required context recall, which aspects would you examine, and what specific metrics would help you identify the root cause of the failure?", "topic": "RAG", "subtopic": "retrieval evaluation", "difficulty": "advanced", "skills": ["context recall analysis", "debugging", "performance metrics"], "expected_concepts": ["context recall and context precision (RAGAS)", "failure analysis by query type", "retrieval tuning"], "follow_up_topics": ["query reformulation techniques", "contextual data improvement", "monitoring retrieval performance"], "evaluation_criteria": ["Identifies context recall as the main metric to inspect", "Considers failure analysis by query type", "Suggests specific retrieval tuning strategies"], "id": "q_196c6a0c43", "source": "llm_generated", "review_status": "pending", "reference_answer": {"key_points": ["Examine the retrieval model's configuration, including parameters like the number of retrieved documents and the similarity threshold.", "Analyze context recall metrics such as Recall@k and Precision@k to assess the effectiveness of the retrieval system.", "Investigate query types that are failing, looking for patterns in low recall cases, such as specific keywords or phrases that are not being matched.", "Utilize tools like Elasticsearch or Pinecone to monitor query performance and retrieval logs for anomalies.", "Consider retraining the model with additional relevant data or fine-tuning hyperparameters to improve recall."], "common_mistakes": ["Focusing solely on precision metrics without considering recall.", "Neglecting to analyze the types of queries that are failing.", "Assuming the model is fine without checking the configuration or tuning parameters."]}, "follow_up_questions": ["What specific metrics do you prioritize when measuring retrieval performance?", "How would you approach retraining the model if recall is consistently low?", "Can you describe a situation where tuning parameters significantly improved retrieval performance?"]}
